    <h3>Your Data Rights</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>You can delete the data collected with your API key at any time</strong> through the Settings page when logged in. 
      You can also <strong>export all your data</strong> in JSON format from the Settings page. 
      Personal data deletion will permanently remove:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>All login sessions and session history</li>
      <li>All API call logs and monitoring data</li>
      <li>Your stored API key</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Faction Data Deletion</h4>
    <p>
      Faction leaders can delete all collected faction data through the Leadership dashboard Settings section.
      Faction data deletion will permanently remove:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>All personal stat snapshots for faction members</li>
      <li>All spy reports collected for the faction</li>
      <li>All ranked war history</li>
      <li>The faction API keys</li>
      <li>The leadership whitelist</li>
      <li>All scheduled background jobs related to the faction (backfill, war polling, etc.)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Subscription time will NOT be revoked</strong> when faction data is deleted. Members keep their 
      remaining subscription time. You can set up the faction again at any time by providing a new API key.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="pp-api-key-security">Your API Key Security</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Important:</strong> Your Torn API key grants access to your game data. Please follow these best practices:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Never share your API key with other individuals</li>
      <li>Only provide your key to trusted, transparent third-party services like TornManager</li>
      <li>Use a Public Only or Limited Access key (not Full Access) when possible</li>
      <li>Monitor your key usage at Torn.com using the 'key' → 'log' selection</li>
      <li>Revoke and regenerate your key if you suspect misuse</li>
      <li>You can pause or delete your API key at any time on Torn.com</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

